ref 17592186045499 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407947 1084 #uuid "f8af2e6f-7f53-52a5-b469-925f72fac328" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407948 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{2}^{8-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dx]dy" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407948 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407948 1084 #uuid "f9c41421-3be2-50e8-9e6b-0a900263854c" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407935 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407940 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407944 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407945 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407946 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1077 "selection" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407946 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407949 1080 #uuid "34f449e1-fb1a-5a4b-9b02-dc697805a6ea" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407931 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407932 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407933 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407947 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407948 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1077 "selection" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407931 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407950 1080 #uuid "90293907-fe9e-585f-8155-9888c4d916c1" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407936 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407937 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407939 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407942 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407943 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1077 "selection" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407939 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407951 1080 #uuid "c010f524-8a53-5bfa-911a-2af5f0f0f3d6" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407929 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407930 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407934 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407938 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407941 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1077 "selection" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407934 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407952 1080 #uuid "ef9310b5-68fe-5622-806f-a4683ba15fec" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407950 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1069 "q-81292" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1071 "![](images/df/df3acf049579ec4de948d84d04d4fe3012c2232b9699d0471857227f52c78107.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $x={y}^{2},\\,$ $x=8-{y}^{2},$ and $y=0,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dA=$" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1072 #uuid "60195b0c-70fb-5843-93ba-a36d5b0f7537" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407953 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2{y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/27/2722224678aeb1f9ea64f42de2dc4fbf6e139350c291de16500957575fd23850.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 8-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{8-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{8-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407952 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1069 "q-37855" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx\\,dy=$" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1072 #uuid "6b2d2a45-1af2-5bb8-b665-008434b3075e" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407954 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407949 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1069 "q-81390" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1071 "![](images/1b/1b03f2ecd03a89d9484e7d28ab4cb34656b288c3a4554c9a4eeacbe9b61f692c.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and $y=2-x,$ above the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1072 #uuid "af73e85d-c908-5a06-97f4-04484193b6c1" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407955 1074 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ y=2-x & \\,⟹\\,x=2-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =2-y \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =(2-y)^{2} \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =4-4y+{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-4y & =0 \\\\ y(y-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=1,$ the $y$-limits are \n$1\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/f8/f8fedf15e26f64fc344bd7db6ffaa659bd7c130f36f4a39389b6108136836104.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,2-y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2-y}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2-y}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{2-y}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{2}[\\,{x}^{2}\\,]_{2-y}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4-{y}^{2}-(2-y)^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,(2y-{y}^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,(2y-{y}^{2})dy & ={[{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(1-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407956 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407960 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407956 1062 #uuid "04ef475a-c5cf-51ff-ad2a-7ea0479c4f76" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407956 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323936 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407957 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407958 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407957 1062 #uuid "1ac49a49-1255-59a8-8c4e-cccd1b1d9a34" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407957 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407953 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407958 1062 #uuid "6b60b51b-f512-550b-bd86-63bfa17217f5" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407958 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407955 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407959 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407957 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407959 1062 #uuid "ac90c75a-a52d-53a2-be62-82bea3febc78" 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407959 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134525 13194139533556 17592186045585 true] [17592186407960 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407959 13194139533556 175921860